cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "kwave-power-law-attenuation-calibration"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible numerical audit of two separate questions in k-Wave: whether a
  literature attenuation coefficient reported for a linear frequency law (y=1)
  is correctly transferred to k-Wave's power-law parameterization at the
  intended operating frequency, and whether the solver then delivers the
  numerical attenuation implied by that transfer. Under a controlled
  homogeneous 1-D setup, matching the coefficient at 0.5 MHz changes the y=2
  calibration error from -50.13% to -0.97%. Near y=1 the failure is not a
  power-law mismatch: at y=1.01 the attenuation deficit is -56.8% to -59.4%
  across 0.2-1.0 MHz with R^2 >= 0.999, i.e. nearly frequency-independent, and
  an independent 3-D control shows a matching +57% excess in peak pressure.
  At y=0.99 the 1-D peak-pressure estimate collapses into numerical residue
  while the 3-D field diverges to order 1e30 Pa.
